==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|la}} {{term|Martialis|lang=la}}, a Roman [[cognomen]] meaning "belonging to [[Mars]]", later also a saint's name.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{given name|male|from=Latin}} narrowly applied to certain [[historic]] persons ( but some of its foreign cognates are modern given names).
# Anglicized [[cognomen]] or [[nickname]] of the [[Roman]] poet Marcus Valerius Martialis, born in [[Spain]] in the first century AD and noted for his [[epigrams]].

